    "description": "A static analysis tool parses Java-like source into a tree of about 40 node types and runs a growing set of analyses over it: dead-code detection, API-usage checks, complexity metrics and a licence-header scan. Every new analysis currently means editing a central switch over node types, and every new node type means touching all analyses; the last parser change broke two analyses that nobody thought about. The analyses need node-specific behaviour plus the ability to accumulate state while walking, and the team wants new analyses as self-contained units that can be shipped and enabled independently. The decision to implement: how to add operations over a fixed hierarchy of node types without editing the node classes, so new analyses do not require touching existing code and node-specific behaviour stays together.",
    "decision_statement": "Add node-type-specific operations over a stable tree hierarchy without modifying the node classes themselves.",
    "notes": "Language switched from rust to java because extensible-visitor is discouraged in rust."
